</ul>
<p style="text-align: center;"><i>"At the end of the Heavenly Demon War, the Aion Tower collapsed. The barrier was not formed amidst distrust, and the clash between the three races swallowed up the light of the world. The tragedy of that day would later be called the 'Last War'."</i></p>
<h3 class="bonfire" id="Gameplay_Features_in_Aion_2">
Gameplay Features in Aion 2</h3><b>Land, Sea, and Air</b>
<ul><li>Traverse a world exponentially larger than that of the original Aion using mounts capable of flight and water traversal.</li></ul>
<p><b>Class System</b>
</p>
<ul><li>Customize your character with character creation and class selection that includes the following eight options: <a href="/Gladiator" title="Gladiator">Gladiator</a>, <a href="/Templar" title="Templar">Templar</a>, <a href="/Assassin" title="Assassin">Assassin</a>, <a href="/Ranger" title="Ranger">Ranger</a>, <a href="/Sorcerer" title="Sorcerer">Sorcerer</a>, <a href="/Elementalist" title="Elementalist">Elementalist</a>, <a href="/Cleric" title="Cleric">Cleric</a>, and <a href="/Chanter" title="Chanter">Chanter</a>.</li></ul>
<p><b>Action-based Combat</b>
</p>
<ul><li>Dodge, block, and strike in real-time with a layered action-oriented combat system. Use chained combos, magic, spirit summons, ranged weaponry, and buffing strategies to bolster your allies as you traverse the open world.</li></ul>
<p><b>PvE</b>
</p>
<ul><li>Join several allies to take on several dungeons across the world for challenging and engaging co-op play.</li></ul>
<p><b>PvP</b>
</p>
<ul><li>Play against others in faction PvP battles. There will be more info to come on this play feature.</li></ul>
</div>
<h3 class="titlearea" id="FAQs">
FAQs</h3>
<div class="row">
<div class="col-sm-6"><h3 class="bonfire" id="When_Does_Aion_2_Release?">
When Does Aion 2 Release?</h3>The game released in Korea and Taiwan in November 19th, 2025. It is currently scheduled for a global release mid-2026.
<h3 class="bonfire" id="What_Kind_of_Setting_Does_Aion_2_Have?">
What Kind of Setting Does Aion 2 Have?</h3>The game is set in the world of Atreia many years following the original game. In this world, players will journey across lands filled with lush vegetation and wild fauna in mystical realms such as Elyos as well as more melancholic and oppressive settings like the Asmodian domain. Players will be able to traverse the land using flight, water traversal, and more from various mounts.
<h3 class="bonfire" id="What_Multiplayer_Options_are_Available?">
What Multiplayer Options are Available?</h3>The game features both PvE and PvP play. Little is yet known about the extent of this options. However, the two primary realms will be warring with one another across PvP matches. Players can then tackle the more difficult challenges the world offers with allies in PvE zones throughout the map. Within each world, there are Expedition events and World events that players can join in teams to fulfill a particular challenge and earn rewards. These events are spread out across the open world.
</div>
<div class="col-sm-6"><h3 class="bonfire" id="Who_is_developing_Aion_2?">
Who is developing Aion 2?</h3>Aion 2 is developed by NCSoft, a South Korean developer responsible for the original 2008 title Aion. The team also worked on such titles like Lineage and Blade &amp; Soul.
<h3 class="bonfire" id="What_Platforms_Will_Aion_2_Be_Available_On?">
What Platforms Will Aion 2 Be Available On?</h3>Aion 2 is currently set to release on PC. Console platforms are unconfirmed.
<h3 class="bonfire" id="Does_Aion_2_Have_a_Class_System?">
Does Aion 2 Have a Class System?</h3>Yes. Aion 2 allows players to select form 8 different classes. Each class offers a different approach to combat and ally support when playing in PvE modes. The classes are as follows: <a href="/Gladiator" title="Gladiator">Gladiator</a>, <a href="/Templar" title="Templar">Templar</a>, <a href="/Assassin" title="Assassin">Assassin</a>, <a href="/Ranger" title="Ranger">Ranger</a>, <a href="/Sorcerer" title="Sorcerer">Sorcerer</a>, <a href="/Elementalist" title="Elementalist">Elementalist</a>, <a href="/Cleric" title="Cleric">Cleric</a>, and <a href="/Chanter" title="Chanter">Chanter</a>. Some classes operate as Tanks like the <a href="/Gladiator" title="Gladiator">Gladiator</a> and <a href="/Templar" title="Templar">Templar</a> while others offer support such as the <a href="/Cleric" title="Cleric">Cleric</a>. <a href="/Ranger" title="Ranger">Rangers</a> can engaged in long-range combat while mage-based classes that include the <a href="/Sorcerer" title="Sorcerer">Sorcerer</a> and <a href="/Elementalist" title="Elementalist">Elementalist</a> can utilize magic and summon spirits as allies respectively.
<br /></div></div>
<h3 class="titlearea" id="Aion_2_Focus_Group_Testing">
Aion 2 Focus Group Testing</h3><p>NCSoft held a Focus Group Test at their Headquarters in South Korea. It was an invite only event, under NDA, however, feedback has been released in various locations and by different means. The testers came from a variety of backgrounds, so feedback is varied and from multiple different perspectives. As part of the test, the players were able to experience the levelling process until around level 21, then were boosted to level 45. Despite some preconceptions, and potential reputational impact from previous developer games and actions, first impressions, world design, and combat system received notably positive reactions overall.
</p>
<p>Please note, the below is summarised key points, gathered through verified testers, streamers, and Korean community chats.

</p>
<div class="row">
<div class="col-sm-6"><h3 class="bonfire" id="General_Impressions">
General Impressions</h3>
<ul><li>Runs on Unreal Engine 5 and features rich, detailed environments.</li>
<li>Customization is flexible, extensive, and true to in-game models.</li>
<li>Combat feels like a hybrid of Aion, Blade &amp; Soul, and Black Desert.</li>
<li>Skill count is limited, partly due to mobile UI design.</li>
<li>Leveling is fast and smooth, with players reaching level 45 easily during the test.</li>
<li>Adventure elements and dungeon rankings offer meaningful progression and rewards.</li>
<li>Exploration is a highlight; hidden dungeons, rich landscapes, and scaling zones keep old areas relevant.</li>
<li>Dungeon re-entry and rerun systems resemble pay-to-win mechanics familiar to Korean audiences.</li>
<li>Crafting materials may be tradable, raising pay-to-win risks.</li>
<li>The devs claim the current monetization is 2–3 months old but may remain unchanged.</li>
<li>Performance was smooth on high-end systems, with rare frame drops during map transitions.</li></ul>
</div>
<div class="col-sm-6"><figure class="mw-halign-center" typeof="mw:File/Frameless"><a href="/File:Aion-2-wiki-world-overview1.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="aion 2 wiki world overview1"><img alt="aion 2 wiki world overview1" src="https://static0.fextralifeimages.com/file/aion2/6/65/Aion-2-wiki-world-overview1.jpg" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="600" height="338" class="mw-file-element" /></a><figcaption>aion 2 wiki world overview1</figcaption></figure></div>
<p><br />
</p>
</div>
<div class="row">
<div class="col-sm-6"><h3 class="bonfire" id="PvE_Specific_Feedback">
PvE Specific Feedback</h3>
<ul><li>Leveling was smooth and enjoyable, with a satisfying progression curve.</li>
<li>Dungeons were cinematic and well-designed, with engaging boss encounters.</li>
<li>Skill chaining felt fluid and fun, especially in party play.</li>
<li>Exploration was rich, with hidden content and a sense of adventure.</li>
<li>4-man party content encouraged cooperation and role synergy.</li>
<li>Combat felt “floaty” or lacked impact, especially with basic attacks.</li>
<li>Some testers found the auto-lock targeting too passive compared to full action systems.</li>
<li>A few felt the controls were awkward; though others suggested it might just come down to player skill.</li>
<li>Early-game tutorials were lacking, likely due to the age of the test build (2–3 months old).</li></ul>
</div>
<div class="col-sm-6"><h3 class="bonfire" id="PvP_Specific_Feedback">
PvP Specific Feedback</h3>
<ul><li>1v1 and 4v4 arenas exist and appeared to be functional.</li>
<li>Class synergy and defined roles were present and received some praise.</li>
<li>Wings disrupt combat; players can escape fights too easily.</li>
<li>Characters die too quickly, making battles feel shallow.</li>
<li>Controls felt overly simplified, reducing depth and skill expression.</li>
<li>No open-world dueling, which disappointed fans of classic Aion.</li>
<li>In general, PvP was seen as “fun in concept, underwhelming in execution.” With improvements to flight mechanics, combat responsiveness, and skill depth, it has potential, but it currently falls short of the expectations set by Aion 1.</li></ul>
</div></div>
<p>Overall, reception among testers is cautiously optimistic: the game has high potential, but UI, combat balance, and monetization need work. NCSoft is targeting a November 11, 2025 release (matching Aion 1’s launch date), though this could shift slightly.

</p>
